2. Methodology

We conducted a series of semi-structured field interviews with senior executives in Australian firms. 2 Interviews are useful in early stage research as a means for identifying key relationships than can later be tested for generalizability (Yin, 2011). Our goal was to conduct a small number of in-depth interviews to derive new insights and to generate hypotheses to test in subsequent phases of this project. As a first step, we conducted a series of pilot interviews with:

market participants;

thought leaders from government-funded organizations and programs (Design Victoria, the Victorian Design Integration Scheme, Enterprise Connect Creative Industries Innovation Centre, Victorian Eco-innovation Lab);

senior executives from government agencies (IP Australia and the Department of Industry);

academics; and

participants involved in the ACIP Review of the Designs System.

